{"diagnosis": "Loopback sent 0xa5 but recv_buf_data latched 0xe0, causing TRAP uart data mismatch. RX start half-bit in state 1 waits 2*recv_divcnt > cfg_divider (half bit), but states default/10 advance when recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4), i.e. 1/16 of a bit period, so recv_pattern shifts ser_rx 16x too fast and samples wrong bit positions.",
"patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -89,14 +89,14 @@
 				10: begin
-					if (recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)) begin
+					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_buf_data <= recv_pattern;
 						recv_buf_valid <= 1;
 						recv_state <= 0;
 					end
 				end
 				default: begin
-					if (recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)) begin
+					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_pattern <= {ser_rx, recv_pattern[7:1]};
 						recv_state <= recv_state + 1;
 						recv_divcnt <= 0;
 					end
 				end",
"expected": "tohost: PASS, loopback recv 0xa5 matches send 0xa5 with no uart data mismatch trap"}

